Z||000001||terryk||01-24-2001||12:33 PM||||Only the 89 and 90 Grand Prix Turbo/STE Turbo||||reg||1
Z||000002||kslish||01-24-2001||06:53 PM||||The Grand Am Turbo had a turbocharged 2.0L 4-cyl in it.  They did away with that engine option once the Quad 4 was available.<P>The Grand Prix Turbo was the only GM model with the 3.1L Turbo and was short lived (available for 3 years I think?) because GM decided they would rather use the 3400 DOHC engine in the top of the line GP's after that.<P>I looked into getting a Grand Prix STE Turbo that had a blown engine a few years back but the parts prices for that engine from GM are unreal.<P>Ken S.<BR>'87 GT and '86 SE<BR> <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A> ||||reg||1
