Z||000005||Slammed Fiero||01-24-2001||09:16 PM||||Sittin here..Lookin at design ones turbo setup ..Looks rather simple. My worry is the use of the stock manifolds with the turbo , any problems forseen there. I have seen Dennis L's setup. In any case I already have a new T# turbo from a merkur (brand new) the mandrel bent stainless tubing is the question<P>Any ideas folks??<P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Predator||01-25-2001||08:55 AM||||I have a Design One Systems Stage II setup. I installed it, but have had some problems. My car had dirty fuel injectors and the head gasket blew. I have it at Engineered Performance and they are fixing it, and to check the setup. Ed the owner has said more than once that the kit is a very well put together kit. Design One uses a GM Map sensor and PROM chip programmed for the turbo with a knock sensor to regulate the air/fuel mixture, and retard the timing under boost. The stock engine can handle it due to the chips controlling everything. After talking to Ed I would not just stick a turbo on it and go. The stock engine cannot handle it unless you have some sort of system to regulate the fuel mixture and timing that is setup specifically for the turbo. The turbo used is a IHI turbo. I don't know much about it other than what Ed said, and that it is a German made turbo and very efficient. He said it is one of the best turbo's you can buy. It is small but packs a good punch, and very reliable. The Design One kit is a little expensive, but you can tell that it is well made and that they don't skimp on the quality of parts, and every time I called Kevin at Design One he was there to answer my questions and always very polite and professional. The Design one system is built to be reliable, but still give you a kick. When it finally gets going again I hope to have them dyno it so I can find out how much power it is making. Design One states around 225 with the Stage II kit, and Ed says that sounds resonable. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Predator (edited 01-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||01-27-2001||08:53 AM||||3.1 i have has forged crank. I used cast iron heads, but there is aluminum too. I heard the aluminum ones breath better. I also used the Fiero intake. My turbo is about the size of a softball. I havent had any problems in over 40K except when it gets really cold below 30 I did have to turn boost down. I run my car pretty hard too. I use reg gas. Lisa drove it, ask her how it runs.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 01-27-2001).]||||reg||1
